 This means that the ``author_id`` column should be a foreign key that references the ``id`` column in the ``authors`` table.
 
+To specify SQLite ``ON DELETE`` or ``ON UPDATE`` behavior, pass a ``ForeignKey`` object. Both actions default to ``NO ACTION``:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from sqlite_utils.db import ForeignKey
+
+    foreign_keys=[ForeignKey(
+        table="books",
+        column="author_id",
+        other_table="authors",
+        other_column="id",
+        on_delete="CASCADE",
+        on_update="RESTRICT",
+    )]
+
+These actions are retained when the table is rebuilt using ``.transform()``, including for compound foreign keys.
+
 You can leave off the third item in the tuple to have the referenced column automatically set to the primary key of that table. A full example:
 
 .. code-block:: python
